  "id": "facial-feedback-hypothesis",
  "term": "facial feedback hypothesis",
  "definition": "The facial feedback hypothesis is the idea that facial muscle activity does not just show emotion but can also shape it by sending signals back to the brain. In this packet, reduced activity of muscles such as the corrugator and procerus is described as altering input to limbic areas and being linked with changes in emotional processing.",
